From: prplMesh virtual-radio lab
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: skip advertised bands without channel data

Some nl80211 radios advertise a band entry whose supported-channel map is
empty.  refresh_radio_info() checked only the first band before dereferencing
the first channel of every band in its frequency-band search.  A tri-band
mac80211_hwsim radio can therefore crash beerocks_fronthaul while attaching
the second and third radios.

Treat a band without channel data as a non-match.  A radio for which every
band is empty still follows the existing failure path instead of
dereferencing an empty container.

--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
@@ -503,6 +503,9 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_nl80211::refresh_radio_info()
     auto band_info_it =
         std::find_if(radio_info.bands.begin(), radio_info.bands.end(),
                      [&](const bwl::nl80211_client::band_info &b) {
+                         if (b.supported_channels.empty()) {
+                             return false;
+                         }
                          return m_radio_info.frequency_band ==
                                 son::wireless_utils::which_freq_type(
                                     b.supported_channels.begin()->second.center_freq);
